###### Abstract

_Early Holocene ice retreat pattern of the Laurentide le Sheet in the Laurentales deiatel man connu. A e'est, la Moraine Maris-Batiscan constitue la seule position frontale continue identifiee entre la Moraine de Saint-Narcisse et la Moraine de Sakami_, Comme la Ceinture morainique de Cartier 1, en Ontario, la Moraine Maris-Batiscan est montau de Saint-Narcisse a la la flui Pisticoene. Le territiore a l'etude est un transect, du Saint-Nature au Temsicamique, qui fait la fonction entre la Moraine Maris-Batiscan et la Peistocene. The study area is a transect between the Riviere Saint-Maurice and the Temsicamique area, roughly in the axis of the Mars-Batiscan and Carrier morines. The application pattern of this transect is based on a systematic mapping of glacial landforms by air photography analysis at a scale of 1:15 840, verified by fieldwork. The glacial margin is bent east of the transect, it becomes relatively linear westward with a WSW-ENE general orientation and several minor locations and re-entrants. The glacial margin was mainly controlled by topography. Depalcation between the latitudinal margins of the transect occurred over a period of 600 years, approximately between 11.46 and 10,86 cal ka (10 000 and 9580 as "C BP). An acceleration of the ice retreat rate occurred after the Mars-Batiscan Moraine phase, followed by relatively stable rates of retreat. The new isochrones improve the previous models of demgication de la region Mattawan-Temsicamique, puisqu'il montre un front de deglaciation lineaire et sans rentrant notable with no visible re-entrant in the axis of the Ottawa River-Temsicamique area during the studied time span._

